Ketil Z Malde (ketil@imr.no) wrote:
> tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at (Thomas Leitner) writes:
>
> Next monday get get a test alpha system with an ATI Mach 64 graphics
> board and want to run it under Digital Unix. In the long run I want to
> use a DEC VRT19-HA fixed frequency monitor with the system.
>

  I doubt that you will be successful.  Having written some of the code
  (it's common source with VMS) I do not believe that there is any way
  to do this in the current driver or server DDX.

  In addition, you will have to deal with both the console and the O/S
  trying to put the monitor into VGA text mode - using the standard
  VESA sync rates.

  The TGA (aka ZLXp-E) was designed from the start with the thought that
  it would be used as a bridge design and customers may have old fixed
  frequency, and sync-on-green monitors.  So it was designed into it.  The
  TGA card does not have a VGA text mode, and it wasn't designed as a PC
  card (though it supports the multi-sync monitors).

  _Fred



