insom@math.ucr.edu (Chris Ulrich) writes:
>   Is there a known problem with dtlogin's ability to generate
> a useful magic cookie?  Every time I log into a particular
> alpha running osf1 3.2 using dtlogin (the silly xdm replacement)
> I get the magic cookie fffffffffffffffffffff which is not very
> useful.  Another machine running xdm does not have this same 
> problem.  Upgrading to 4.0 is not an option.

We submitted bug reports on this for just about every version prior to
the 4.0 release (where it was finally fixed).  The solution is to not
use dtlogin with any version of OSF prior to 4.0.  If you want CDE,
run xdm and have your .xsession start CDE, but don't run dtlogin
itself unless you are behind a firewall and trust everyone behind it,
because it leaves your X session wide open.

>   Dec seems to have really bad quality control.  First their 
> automounter doesnt work at all, and this as well.

In their defense, DEC doesn't claim that CDE in 3.2 is a production
release--it is explicitly packaged as an advanced developer's kit, not
a production version.
