I remember an announcement some time ago of prelim manuals for converting
step 1 to step 2 drivers and so on on the net. Those have been on some
of the DECUS VMS/L&T SIG tapes, many of which are available at 
either ftp.decus.org or www.decus.org.(The latter works for anon ftp
access too.)
Such manuals may also be available someplace in the www.digital.com
tree also.

As for some of the hardware manuals, I don't have any special info. Note
there are a bunch of .digital.com websites around though (service.digital.com...

and many more). It might not hurt to see if, say, Altavista has any info
it can help find.

My experience going step1 to step2 is that the changes can mostly be
made rather mechanically, but the more complex the device the harder
the changes in the interface can be.

As for "cpu" manuals, you must remember that there's a separate part
of the code called "cpu code" here and sometimes people drift into
their own everyday-used jargon. The "cpu code" is different for every
platform basically and implements very low level interfaces so that
everything else (pretty much) does not have to worry about the differences.

Different sites use different words for this kind of stuff, and in general
the "cpu code" (as the term is used here) sits below device drivers
logically and is used by them a fair bit just to avoid maintenance logistical
problems.

Glenn



