In article <x7iv806cgi.fsf@shelby.mst6.lanl.gov> Dave Carter
<carter@lanl.gov> wrote:
[deleted post regarding a new requirement for a licence to use
a sequential access loader with NetWorker V4.2A on Digital UNIX]

For others who may be interested in the response sent to
Dave, below is a statement from the Product Manager, 
posted with permission.

It is true that with V4.2A of NetWorker for Digital UNIX, a jukebox license
is required for sequential access loaders.  As you probably know, Digital
OEMs NetWorker from Legato System Inc.  Legato has over 10 OEMs and Digital
is the  only vendor who has not charged for sequential access.  Last year
we reviewed our pricing with the rest of the backup market and felt we
offered an exceptional value for the product.  The effort we put in to
support (code) and test changers is essentially the same regardless of
whether the device is used as a sequential- or auto-changer.  To be able to 
continue to offer a broad range of device support (device qualification is
a large portion of our testing budget) and to be competitive in the market,
we felt charging for this functionality was warranted.

Regards,
Salley Anderson
NetWorker Product Manager





