organization: Flying Disk Systems, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.org.decus,comp.sys.dec


I got an annoying telemarketing call this morning from DEC.
The caller (Keven Reed, 800-277-8988 x4485) wanted to know
if I was going to register for the fall DECUS symposium.
I was annoyed for three reasons:

1) I had already registered and received a confirmation.

2) When I sent in the form, I checked the box that says
   I DO NOT WANT the information released to exhibitors
   (I assume that this would include DEC).

3) I had told DEC in the past that I did not want telemarketing
   calls.

I asked to speak to his supervisor, who he informed me
was Judy Lynch, 800-277-8988 x4476.   After complaining
to her about being called, I tried to press the issue of
DEC calling people who had already registered and received
confirmation.   She did not have an answer.   I asked
to speak to her supervisor.   Instead, she said that she
was ending the call and hung up.

After two calls, I finally managed to speak to Bill Keese,
the manager of telemarketing (508-952-3306).   I explained
why I was upset at the call, and he agreed that there was
a problem with calling people who had already registered,
and that they would discontinue calling DECUS members until
the problem was resolved.   However, he told me that the
reason Judy Lynch gave him for terminating the call was that
I had used profanity to her!   Fortunately, they tape record
these calls so I expect that this will have a negative impact
on her next performance review, after they review the tape.

I am concerned that DEC "lost" the fact that I don't want
telemarketing calls.

I am also concerned that DECUS is giving my membership
information to DEC to use for telemarketing.

I am very concerned that a DEC employee would try to
cover herself by falsely claiming that a customer used
profanity.

How low can DEC sink?

Bill Keese is responsible for these telemarketers, so you
should call him at 508-952-3306 if you object to DEC's
telemarketing calls.    Unfortunately, I do not have his
e-mail address.

--  Alan E. Frisbie               Frisbie@Flying-Disk.Com
--  Flying Disk Systems, Inc.



