Ack!  We have a couple of old MicroVAX IIs that we are trying to set up as
shell account servers (our school took away shell account access).  Right
now, they are both running Ultrix 4.1, which is what the school used to
use as their main mail server back in 1990-91.

In order to have something that we know better, we're trying to set up the
vax port of NetBSD, but we're having problems in one of the steps.  After
following all the instructions from both the install readmes in the BSD
archive to the NetBSD/VAX FAQ, we're having a problem and we don't know
why:

We can run edlabel and copy fine from the BSD boot tape (TK50 method) and
we can even do a 3rd restart to boot the miniroot on from the hard drive. 
However, when we get to the prompt that asks "Root device?" (the FAQ says
you're supposed to enter raxx* here, xx being the device) we can't get any
further.  Either we're dumped into assembly and can't continue and must
reboot, or we get some kind of error message saying that the root
partition can't be found or whatever.

Anyone who's done this and is willing to lend a hand would be greatly
appreciated.  Please e-mail me.

Thanks in advance for your help,

-- Jeremy

