In article <1996Oct2623.54.28.11110@koobera.math.uic.edu>,
D. J. Bernstein <djb@koobera.math.uic.edu> wrote:
>David Hull <dhull@gsu.edu> wrote:
>> SCSI can go up to 40 MB/s with conventional controllers
>
>Yeah, sure, with drives spinning at about 54,000 RPM.

Or with multiple disks.

Suppose you swap onto 6 disks on the same SCSI channel.
The physical disk can take at most 5M/sec of data, say,
as a reasonable hypothetical number.

Each individual disk has that max throughput, but
the SCSI channel--and swapping, can move at up to 36M/s.

Furthermore, disks often have hardware caches these days.
Communication with the disk cache can be much quicker than
the physical disk could support.

PM



