Robert Phillips <rphilips@erols.com> writes:

>If the SC21 is a DMA sevice you need to disconnect the DMA continuity 
>jumper on the backplane.  Somewhere in the documentation is the location, 
>I no longer remember it by heart.

Jumpers are on the back side (the wiring side) of the backplane.  The
jumper is between pins CA1 and CB1.  On some backplanes, they are
wire-wrapped and have to be cut (or otherwise removed) without affecting
surrounding wires.  I have seen, however, some systems with the NPG
jumper as a real jumper which can be removed and re-installed.

