In article <326743F3.7045@atlas.uvigo.es>, Aula de Informatico de Teleco <aitel@atlas.uvigo.es> writes:
> 	I have a Vaxstation 2000, but the bad news are that I have no power 
> supply. So can i use one from a PC?. Does anybody know the pinout of 
> that 9 pin squake conector?

1, 2, 3 = GND
4 = -12V
5,6 = +5V
7 = +12V
8 = -9V return (probably hooked to ground)
9 = -9V

The -9V supply is required for the thinwire Ethernet. Since a PC power
supply doesn't provide -9V, you probably won't be able to hook up a PC
supply.
