for them.)

My take on all this is that we're still recovering from the losses from
1992-1994.  I started (well, resumed) here in the quarter of our largest
loss.  It's been interesting watching the company change from what worked
for us in the 1980s to what the industry was changing into in the, uh, 1980s.

There's more to do, but heck, there's always more to do!

Definitely a good week to be an engineer insted of upper management or
public relations.
