Given lower sales/employee, you can either reduce the number of
employee's or increase the sales.


One problem Digital has is in packaging their systems. For example, if
you buy new DEC workstations or even 4100's, the default ethernet
controller is *still* a 21040 10BaseT ethernet. In a $100,000 machine
they should bite the bullet and spend the extra $10 to put in fast
ethernet.

For other reasons, take a look at how an SGI system is packaged.
Although the SGI Indy is slower than molassas for computational work,
it comes with built-in support for video-conferencing and reasonable
3D graphics tools.  Only in the last year or so has Digital started
shipping OpenGL as a stanfard tool. You still can't get an Alpha that
can do MBONE or conferencing w/o spending gobs of extra money.

This stuff may be marginally important to some segment of the market,
but it's the kind of stuff that attracts some buyers.

-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



