Thanks to everyone who responded so quickly and in particular to Doug
Mallory (dlm@io.org) who wrote:

>This sounds like the classic ,"did you remove the NPG jumper on the 
>backplane?" question.
>When you moved the module from the expansion unit to the CPU box, you probably 
>removed a grant card (G727) and installed the controller there. If the NPG 
>jumper for that slot is in, no DMA requests will work for this board and will 
>give you that CP HUNG message.
>The NPG jumper is between pins CA1 and CB1 on each slot that has no DMA 
>controller in it, if you remove this wire, all should work O.K. , as you said 
>RSX sees the devices there.

While I can't say that I fully understand what this means, removing the
jumper between these two pins now means that we can access the disks
again.

Thanks again,
Rob

