I have DEC Alpha 600 workstations running OSF/1 V3.2D and they are
connected to the a network printer using HP JetDirect printer server.

If I were to send two large ASCII files consecutively to the printer
from one of the DEC, the second print job will be corrupted; only the
last few lines were printed. I contacted DEC support from my country
and, as expected, they were quick to put the blame on the printer
server. I then conducted the following tests.

1.  If I were to again sent two large ASCII files consecutively to the
printer as before, but on two separate DEC workstations instead of one,
the second print job completed as without any problems.

2.  If I were to send a postscript file and an ASCII file consecutively,
again the second print job complete without any problem. (The same
network printer was configured as two different printers; one as text
and another as raw. As such, the postscript file went to the raw printer
queue and the ASCII file went to the text queue)

3. If I were to sent two ASCII files to the printer from the PC network,
again I have no problems.


So my questions are:

Has anyone experienced the same problem as me?

Based on all the tests done by me, can I conclude that there is no
problem with the printer server? I feel that as far as the printer
server is concern, it makes no difference if the print job is from one
or more workstations. The printer merely accepts printer job if the
printer buffer is not full. Am I right?

Any comments are appreciated. Thanks in  advance.

Lu Chun



