|Having trouble finding throughput and other ratings on these
|equiptment. Can't figure what is triggering the loss. Some time-out
|feature? The loss definitely occurs at the repeater.  Same situation
|with same hardware in two different countries.
|
|Anyone have any ideas?

First, Ethernet repeaters don't have "throughput" ratings.
They all operate at the bit level, and have a "throughput"
of exactly 10Mbps, no more, no less.  

As repeaters operate at the bit level, frame sizes don't
really mean much to them.  A condition when a large number
of large frames are destroyed, while small frames get thru
OK, is typically associated with an invalid Ethernet.
(Segments too long, too many repeaters, etc.)  I would definitely
map out my Ethernet and verify all segments.

Of course, it could be that the DECrepeater 90 is malfunctioning 
- someone who has experience with them (i.e. not me) might be able
to say whether it has any known problems in this area.

