In article <54io6p$r5c@rzunews.unizh.ch>,
   carter@pci.unizh.ch (Rob Carter) wrote:
>
>
>However...  The PDP has two Fujitsu 2284N hard discs.  Recently the
>machine died and these disks could not be accessed.  The problem was
>tracked down to a failure in an expansion box containing the disk
>controller.  On moving the disk controller to the main case, we are now
>in the position of having the controller being recognised on booting
>and DEV showing the existence of the two DR: disks.  However on trying
>to mount these disks, the CPU hangs.  Likewise if we try to boot from
>DR0:, the CPU hangs.
>
>
>The disk controller is labelled Emulex ASSY SU 2110401 with firmware
>SC2110201-8ME.  We are running RSX-11M.  Thanks in advance for any help. 
>Cheers, 
>Rob Carter
>
This sounds like the classic ,"did you remove the NPG jumper on the 
backplane?" question.
When you moved the module from the expansion unit to the CPU box, you probably 
removed a grant card (G727) and installed the controller there. If the NPG 
jumper for that slot is in, no DMA requests will work for this board and will 
give you that CP HUNG message.
The NPG jumper is between pins CA1 and CB1 on each slot that has no DMA 
controller in it, if you remove this wire, all should work O.K. , as you said 
RSX sees the devices there.

Good Luck..

	-Doug-



