	      Digital's StrongARM Microprocessors Post Top
		CaffeineMark Scores for JAVA Performance

  MAYNARD, Mass., October 17, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
  today announced that its StrongARM SA-110 microprocessor has 
  achieved the highest published scores for the CaffeineMark 2.01 
  interpreted Java applet performance benchmark, in comparison to 
  well-known desktop systems.  The StrongARM results were obtained 
  with a prototype Internet terminal, a reference hardware design for 
  the StrongARM SA-110 chip that was used to port the JavaOS operating 
  system to the StrongARM architecture.

       Pendragon Software's CaffeineMark is a benchmark applet, 
  written in the Java language, which rates the performance of Java 
  applets by specific hardware-software configurations. Using JavaOS 
  and the Hot Java browser, the tests were conducted by Digital 
  Equipment Corporation's Systems Research Center and results were 
  verified by Richard Black, an independent consultant from Cambridge 
  University.
      
  StrongARM Terminal Beats Desktops

       Digital Internet terminal configurations with 233MHz and 185MHz 
  StrongARM microprocessors, running JavaOS and the Hot Java browser, 
  produced interpreted CaffeineMark scores more than twice as high as 
  a Silicon Graphics Indigo Extreme 2 workstation (MIPS R4400-250MHz 
  CPU, Irix 5.3 OS), a Sun Ultra 170 workstation (UltraSPARC-167MHz 
  CPU, Solaris 2.5 OS), and an AT-compatible Pentium Pro-200MHz PC 
  (Linux OS), all running Netscape Navigator 2.0 or 3.0b5a. The 233MHz 
  StrongARM SA-110 Internet terminal thus has the highest published 
  CaffeineMark numbers for interpreted Java performance.
      
  Industry's Best Price/Performance

       "The CaffeineMark scores demonstrate that the StrongARM 
  SA-110 interprets Java applets extremely fast and is well suited
  for low-cost Java appliances with small memory footprints," said 
  Leo Joseph, Internet appliance marketing manager for Digital 
  Semiconductor.  "We are also working on a JIT (Just In Time) 
  compiler for StrongARM that will give a performance improvement of 
  ten times for the CaffeineMark benchmark.  At sub-watt power levels 
  and prices below $50, StrongARM chips deliver the industry's leading 
  MIPS-per-dollar and MIPS-per-watt for embedded applications."

       CaffeineMark results and information about the CaffeineMark 
  benchmark can be viewed at the CaffeineMark website at:  
  http://www.webfayre.com/pendragon/cm2/index.html.

       Developed under license from Advanced RISC Machines Ltd., the 
  StrongARM microprocessor is now in volume production with speed/
  performance options ranging from 100MHz/115 MIPS to 233MHz/270 MIPS.  
  Input voltage beginning at 1.65 volts enables low power dissipation 
  and the industry's best performance-to-power ratios.  StrongARM 
  SA-110 microprocessors range in price from $29 to $49 in quantities 
  of 10,000.

