>How does a MicroVax 3300 compare to a Pentium 166 based system? What
>about the MV3300 vs a dual P-Pro 200 system?

Well, the MicroVAX can run VMS or ULTRIX, which the Pentium system
can't do.  To its credit the Pentium probably can run any number
of modern UNIX systems and will be much faster than the MicroVAX.

In a decade where microprocessor performance has improved two orders
of magnitude, systems of the 3300's class have pitifully slow
performance compared to modern systems.  Still, the MicroVAX 3300
isn't quite *that* old, but it is much slower than either Intel
based system.

