 It is not clear to me that we provide traditional technical
 documentation on all of our system platforms.  With perhaps the
 exception of the Evaluation Board kits from Digital Semiconductor.

 Very little of it would be of use to you unless you were going to
 write the platform support code - as opposed to a device driver.

 The device driver manual is the primary source of information on
 developing a device driver for VMS.  I would also strongly
 recommend "Writing OpenVMS Alpha Device Drivers in C" by Margie
 Sherlock and Lenny Szubowicz (Digital Press ISBN 1-55558-133-1).
 You will find the information I think you are looking for in the
 appendices.

 In addition, you may (but are unlikely to) need bus specifications
 such as the PCI specs, EISA specs, etc.  And you of course mostly
 need the HW specifications for the *device* you are writing the
 driver for. 

