Digital's OpenVMS Version 7.1 External Field Test 2 (EFT2) Software
Developer's Kit (SDK) is now available!  

The SDK contains early releases of the OpenVMS V7.1 VAX and Alpha 
operating systems. The kit will allow OpenVMS software developers 
early access to the new features and enhancements of V7.1.  For 
details on the new features and enhancements provided in V7.1, 
refer to:

  http://www.openvms.digital.com/os/ovmsv71_functionality.html.

In addition to the operating system, users can also test compatible
layered product kits that will be made available on the Internet at
the same time.  

The SDK software will run on all Alpha and VAX systems currently 
shipping.  The SDK is intended for development testing only.  It 
should not be used in a production environment.  Please refer to 
the SDK CD-ROM Booklet for a list of new features in the release 
and for a complete description of the kit contents.  

The SDK package contains all necessary firmware, documentation, and 
temporary product authorization keys (PAKs) necessary to take full 
advantage of V7.1.  The temporary PAKs will allow use of the software
until January 1997. 

Those who have already registered with Digital to receive a copy of the 
V7.1-EFT2 SDK should expect to receive the CD-ROM kit in the 7-10 days.
Those who have not registered to receive the SDK can send their request 
to: 
        sdk@star.enet.dec.com

Support for SDK users will be through an Internet newsgroup 
(vmsnet.sdk.openvms.fieldtest) to report problems, make comments, etc.  
An engineering support team will monitor the newsgroup and address any 
issues.  Note that this is the ONLY support method for the SDK.  
Although SDK support will be provided until January 1997, when the SDK
PAKs expire, we encourage you to report problems within the first several 
weeks in order for your feedback to have the most impact on the release. 

We will make every effort to respond to you in a timely manner, but in 
the unlikely event you do not receive a response within 4 working days, 
please contact any member of the SDK team via direct e-mail:

