Trip Martin wrote:
> 
> I've heard that VMS won't run on a Multia, but the ROM monitor
> mentions VMS in addition to Digital Unix and NT.  And since
> the monitors are very machine specific, that doesn't make
> much sense.  Anyone know the real story?
>

  The console firmware for OpenVMS and Unix is common code from
  a pool maintained by the hardware development groups.  This
  console (called the SRM console internally) uses the OpenVMS
  PALcode image to operate, and is in fact capable of booting
  OpenVMS - if it existed for the hardware platform.

  They would in fact need to go out of their way to expunge the
  ability to boot OpenVMS.

  That does *not* imply that OpenVMS is, or ever will be made
  available on the Multia.  There are about a dozen threads here,
  and in the VMS news groups on this topic.  VMS does not run
  because due to business decisions, not due to any technical
  reasons.

_Fred



