This is more or less how I run my MicroVAX 3100.

> 
> What is the best way to go about this?
> 
> There is no obvious "console" port; just a regular and printer
> MMF connector.  I opened the system up and removed the VS40X
> (8-plane graphics board) thinking that, like a Q-Bus MicroVAX/
> VAXstation, if it didn't detect the graphics hardware it would
> "revert" to a non-graphical system.  However having tried that
> and having connected a VT320 to the two serial ports and having
> nothing happen, I suspect that might not be the way to do it.

Plug your terminal into the MMJ port marked printer. There should be a switch 
somewhere around there that points the console firmware to either the video 
system or the serial port. Move this switch to point it to the serial port. 
Boot the VAX.

I suspect it is a bit of a bum steer trying to get X output from the console 
port. I do not know the interns of VMS well enough to suggest how you do this 
but you might want to try put PPP over one of the other serial ports and get 
your X through there. The simplest method though would be to get X over a 
network. Put UCX or some other IP stack on the VMS system and an IP stack on 
the PC and off you go.

