Todd, 

The Starion 500 had a Pentium 60 processor in a ZIF socket (socket 4
type), 256K cache, flashable Phoenix BIOS (non PnP despite ref's in
setup screens), 8MB RAM, and C&T Wingine video all integrated on the
main board.  It can be upgraded with Intel Pentium Overdrive
processors & standard 70ns 32-bit (non-parity) SIMMS via 4 SIMM slots.
The p/n for the Starion 400/500 users guide is ER-902AA-UA and can be
ordered through 1-800-DIGITAL if they're still available.

You can obtain toll-free hardware phone support at 1-800-554-3333,
press option 1.  I hope this info is useful to you.

