Carl Follstad wrote:
> 
> We recently purchased two AlphaServer 4100 and a AlphaServer 2000.  All
> three machines were purchased with CIPCAs in them to allow them to
> participate in our existing (VAX) VMScluster.  We've had two outright
> failures on the CIPCAs (we've had them about 6 weeks in our test cluster)
> and have replaced one suspect board.

  What were the "outright failures".  If they were failures then why has
only
  "one suspect board" been replaced.  Which module (or set) was
replaced?

  A better understanding of what "failure" means would help.

> Also, about 3 weeks ago I moved the
> 2000 into our production cluster and all seemed OK until last week when we
> had an unexplained cluster hang (some systems responded but all cluster
> resources seemed unavailable to all other systems).  We had to reset all
> systems to get production running and no crash dump was forced before we
> reset and rebooted so my diagnostic information is limited.

  My concern here is how were the machines "added" to an existing
cluster?

  Live?  If so, were the VAXen re-AUTOGEN'd for the cluster increase?  
  Many SCS parameters are allowed to grow but NPAGEDYN can get in the
way of the
  expansion.  A critical parameter here is SCSCONNCNT.  It is dynamic
under
  AXP but not on VAX.

  Also, what versions of VMS were you running?  CIPCA's require 6.2-1H2
min and the
  the 4100 has a min of (6.2-1h?)  What version of VAX/VMS were you
running?

> 
> Has anyone else had similar experienced with CIPCAs or AlphaServer
> 2000s?  Maybe I'm unfairly suspecting these new systems but nothing else
> has changed in the cluster for a couple months (I replaced a bunch of CI
> cables then).

  You are right in suspecting the new systems because that was the last
variable
  changed.  But as for the H/W that may be a different story.  Much of
what 
  can cause problems like this is overall OS configuration as much as
bad H/W.

> 
> Any other ideas?
> 

  What is your cluster configuration look like?  How many nodes?  What
Node Id's?
  What are your other CI Adapters (type)?  What kind of Storage
controllers do 
  you have in the cluster?

  Most imporantly, any errorlogs?  Primarily, PA and PN.
	
