Yes, I've done it.
It wouldn't work on an older DS700 we have in the office, but it did
work on a customer's more recent DS700.
I can't remember off-hand what EPROM revision level is required.
And it doesn't just work to download the WWENG2.SYS from a MOP server
either, I tried the same downline load image with 2 different DS700's.

If you can get admin access to the DS700, there should be online
help which describes PPP config commands if it's supported.

An alternative is to use SLIP, which is supported on the older DS700,
and UCX 3.3 and up now supports SLIP, even on a LAT port created for
a DS700 port.

Right now I've got a USR 33.6 Sportster hanging off TTA0: of an
AlphaStation 255, VMS 6.2-something, UCX 4.0, SLIP port, works.

Bookreader docs on the Layered Products CDs completely explain
how to set up PPP port on DS700.

Hope this helps.


