>as well as the www.specbench.org site and was unable to find anything
>on this line.  My desire is to be able to say (for example) that the 
>DEC 3000/300 is roughly equivalent to a HP J210 or a Sun Ultra 170, etc.

Dear Sir,

  A DEC 3000/300 is not comparable to an HP J210 or a Sun Ultra 170.
An analogy would be comparing a 486 to a Pentium.

  A DEC 3000/300 is about as powerful as a 133MHz pentium in floating
point,  and inferior in integer.

Here are some SPEC92 benchmarks.  DEC has never bothered running
SPEC95 on the DEC 3000/300 since it is so outdated.

System            CPU        ClkMHz  Cache      SPECint SPECfp  Info  Source
Name              (NUMx)Type ext/in  Ext+I/D      92      92    Date  Obtained
================= ========== ======= ========== ======= ======= ===== =========
DEC 3000/300      A21064     30/150  256+8/8      66.2    91.5  Apr93 c.sun.mc
DEC 3000/300L     A21064     20/100  256+8/8      45.9    63.6  Apr93 c.sun.mc
HP J210           PA7200    120      256/256     168.7   269.2  Jun95 www.hp
Sun Ultra1/170    UltraSP    83/167  512+16/16   252     351    Nov95 SunIntro
Intel Xpress      Pentium    66/133  512+8/8     147.5   109.6  Jun95 www.intel

This is an example of more current DEC technology:
DEC 600/5/333     A21164     83/333  4M+96+8/8   412.4   545.2  Jan96 Digital

Though you should use  SPEC95 to compare machines for sale nowadays.


PeterM




