-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

 I've ported TGD, written by Bradley K. Sherman, to VMS for VAX and Alpha. TGD
reads in text files containing commands to write out GIF files. It can be used
with plain text files, or in conjunction with Perl or some other scripting
language if you want to do clever stuff. This makes it ideal for creating
dynamic GIFs for Web Servers such as the OSU DECthreads HTTP Server. The TGD
.ZIP file, available from the "Public Domain Software" link on my web page
http://www.pottsoft.demon.co.uk/ includes source for Tom Boutell's GD library,
required by TGD. Follow the links to Tom and Bradley's pages for extra
documentation.

Compile by setting default to the TGD directory and typing MMK or MMS.
(MMK is available from ftp.wku.edu ). The TGD command is set up by 

$ @PDS$DISK:[PDS.TGD1_2B]SETUP
      ^       ^
      |       |
      +---+---+
          |
        Insert your location here

  It detects the architecture and expects the VAX executable to be called
TGD.EXE, and the Alpha executable to be renamed as TGD.EXE_ALPHA, and both to
be living in the same directory as SETUP.COM .

                    - Phil Ottewell

