You're probably better off without any of the DEC debuggers anyways.  
They don't work well on programs which are running, and they don't 
provide any support for core files.  Unless you mean they write their own!

We've been complaining to DEC for 2 years about the quality of these 
products and they have done zilch.  It certainly provides interesting 
insights into whey OSF/1 and the layered products are not solid 
products.  How can you build a solid product with a useless debugger?

I still remember when DEC built solid software.


