In article <52qp50$rs2@lyra.csx.cam.ac.uk>, ard12@eng.cam.ac.uk (A.R. Duell) writes:
>>Um, what is the story with the Qbus-UNIBUS perverter found on 11/84s & 
>>/94s?
> 
> I _thought_ that sat on the PMI rather than the Q-bus, and couldn't (say) 
> be used with an 11/23 CPU. Also, does it behave correctly if there are 
> (say) DMA devices on both the Unibus and the Processor's Q-bus? It wasn't 
> (AFAIK) a supported configuration.

Yes, it sits on the PMI. You can have _no_ devices on the QBus, DMA or not.
I once tried sliding a DLV11-J into the Qbus; the processor didn't even see it.

There's a jumper on the processor module to indicate whether it's a QBus or
UNIBUS system. I suspect that if the module is jumpered for a UNIBUS system, 
all I/O page traffic is redirected over the PMI and doesn't even show up 
on the QBus. I don't recall whether I ever hooked up a logic analyzer to 
see if this is true, though...
