> craig> printcap:
> craig> ---------
> craig> # LaserWriter 16/600 PS in Dole 3090
> craig> lp|lp0|0|spedlab:\
> craig> :lf=/var/adm/lperr:\
> craig> :lp=:\
> craig> :of=/usr/lib/filters/lf2crlf:\
> craig> :rm=spedlab:\
> craig> :rp=spedlab:\
> craig> :sd=/var/spool/spedlab:
> 
>> Remote printer queues don't run filters on the local machine.  The filter will
>> have to be placed on spedlab.

The suggested solution is impossible if the printer has a built-in
TCP/IP inteface like HP LaserJet 4M.
To solve the problem install enscript, the gnu version of Adobe
TranScript, written by Markku Rossi, and redefine the commands lpr using
an alias like:
alias lpr '/usr/local/bin/enscript --fancy-header=a2ps -DDuplex:true -Z
$*'

see the manual for definitions.

With -Z enscript work as a filter for ascii and postscript files and $*
pass the lpr parameter to enscript.
