Are you interested in an enterprise-wide printing solution, then try out
NQM at http://www.dimatrix.dk/dist/distribution.html

NQM - Network Queue Management, is a comprehensive package for output
management, spooling and accounting in a mixed network environment.
NQM supports bi-directional filtering and printing (any file-type) to
devices like:
	HP-LaserJet using PJL, Direct TCP
	QMS Crown using DOC, Direct TCP and TTY
	Any TTY device
	Print servers (Microplex, Axis, Lantronix, Xyplex, Emulex)
	Customized device driver
drived from one or more NQM print servers:
	HP-UX
	DEC/Unix
	Solaris and SunOS
	AIX
and available as clients:
	MS-Windows (interacts gracefully w Print Manager)
	VAX & AXP / VMS
	The above Unix platforms

NQM is based on one central broker, distributed print servers and
distributed clients. NQM operates using advanced RPC techniques that
allows a single job to be routed (for rendering etc) across different
CPU's before terminating (typically printing). The configuration is
done centrally through a Motif GUI.

NQM is now offered to the public under a limited license. For many
users, this implies that you can use it free of charge. For commercial
users, you are expected to donate a small fee (see copyright notice in
the above mentioned web address). Source code licenses can be arranged.

