>How does one create a bootable, complete, backup of MicroVMS 4.6?
>More specifically, can a bootable magtape of MicroVMS 4.6 be made
>using a TS05 tape drive?   

It probably can and has been done, but I don't think it's a vanilla
version of standalone backup that will do what you want.  In particular,
I don't think the KA630 knows how to boot a MS:-class device.  There
are probably further impedements as well (lack of a MS: boot block,
perhaps.)

If you put your TS05 (basically a Pertec-formatted interface tape
drive) on something like a Emulex QT13, it could then be a TMSCP-class
device and you could definitely boot off of it - I've done this.

>For creating a bootable tape, I'm guessing that I'd need to use the
>sysgen program.  I ran it, and looked through the help files for it,
>but that didn't help very much.

No.  SET DEF SYS$UPDATE: and then @STABACKIT.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



